{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:21357332 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:21357332 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"21357332","source":"MED","pmid":"21357332","doi":"10.1542/peds.2010-3852","title":"Fever and antipyretic use in children.","authorString":"Section on Clinical Pharmacology and Therapeutics, Committee on Drugs, Sullivan JE, Farrar HC.","authorList":{"author":[{"collectiveName":"Section on Clinical Pharmacology and Therapeutics"},{"collectiveName":"Committee on Drugs"},{"fullName":"Sullivan JE","lastName":"Sullivan","firstName":"Janice E","initials":"JE"},{"fullName":"Farrar HC","lastName":"Farrar","firstName":"Henry C","initials":"HC"}]},"investigatorList":{"investigator":[{"fullName":"Sullivan JE","lastName":"Sullivan","firstName":"Janice E","initials":"JE"},{"fullName":"Frick GS","lastName":"Frick","firstName":"Glen S","initials":"GS"},{"fullName":"Maxwell LG","lastName":"Maxwell","firstName":"Lynne G","initials":"LG","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4406-9232"}},{"fullName":"Paul IM","lastName":"Paul","firstName":"Ian M","initials":"IM","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6344-8609"}},{"fullName":"Pope JF","lastName":"Pope","firstName":"John F","initials":"JF"},{"fullName":"Wells TG","lastName":"Wells","firstName":"Thomas G","initials":"TG"},{"fullName":"Frattarelli DA","lastName":"Frattarelli","firstName":"Daniel A C","initials":"DA"},{"fullName":"Galinkin JL","lastName":"Galinkin","firstName":"Jeffrey L","initials":"JL"},{"fullName":"Green TP","lastName":"Green","firstName":"Thomas P","initials":"TP"},{"fullName":"Hegenbarth MA","lastName":"Hegenbarth","firstName":"Mary A","initials":"MA"},{"fullName":"Hudak ML","lastName":"Hudak","firstName":"Mark L","initials":"ML"},{"fullName":"Knight ME","lastName":"Knight","firstName":"Matthew E","initials":"ME"},{"fullName":"Shaddy RE","lastName":"Shaddy","firstName":"Robert E","initials":"RE"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4406-9232"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6344-8609"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"127","journalIssueId":1811940,"dateOfPublication":"2011 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2011,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Pediatrics","title":"Pediatrics","essn":"1098-4275","issn":"0031-4005","isoabbreviation":"Pediatrics","nlmid":"0376422"},"printPublicationDate":"2011-03-01"},"pubYear":"2011","pageInfo":"580-587","abstractText":"Fever in a child is one of the most common clinical symptoms managed by pediatricians and other health care providers and a frequent cause of parental concern. Many parents administer antipyretics even when there is minimal or no fever, because they are concerned that the child must maintain a \"normal\" temperature. Fever, however, is not the primary illness but is a physiologic mechanism that has beneficial effects in fighting infection. There is no evidence that fever itself worsens the course of an illness or that it causes long-term neurologic complications. Thus, the primary goal of treating the febrile child should be to improve the child's overall comfort rather than focus on the normalization of body temperature. When counseling the parents or caregivers of a febrile child, the general well-being of the child, the importance of monitoring activity, observing for signs of serious illness, encouraging appropriate fluid intake, and the safe storage of antipyretics should be emphasized. Current evidence suggests that there is no substantial difference in the safety and effectiveness of acetaminophen and ibuprofen in the care of a generally healthy child with fever. There is evidence that combining these 2 products is more effective than the use of a single agent alone; however, there are concerns that combined treatment may be more complicated and contribute to the unsafe use of these drugs. Pediatricians should also promote patient safety by advocating for simplified formulations, dosing instructions, and dosing devices.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Review","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Fever","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PP","qualifierName":"physiopathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Body Temperature","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Child"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Antipyretics","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TU","qualifierName":"therapeutic use"}]}}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Antipyretics","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Free after 12 months","availabilityCode":"F12","documentStyle":"html","site":"intl-pediatrics.aappublications.org","url":"http://intl-pediatrics.aappublications.org/cgi/content/full/127/3/580"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"abs","site":"intl-pediatrics.aappublications.org","url":"http://intl-pediatrics.aappublications.org/cgi/content/abstract/127/3/580"},{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1542/peds.2010-3852"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":244,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMA